1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,427
Today is September 19, 2026.

3
00:00:07,427 --> 00:00:15,037
Overnight, risk assets staged a full-blown short squeeze rally after the Fed landed its first rate hike in three years.

4
00:00:15,037 --> 00:00:20,209
The S and P five hundred, Nasdaq, and Dow all closed higher.

5
00:00:20,209 --> 00:00:24,988
The ten-year Treasury yield broke below four point nine seven percent.

6
00:00:24,988 --> 00:00:28,959
That snapped an eight-day losing streak for bond prices.

7
00:00:28,959 --> 00:00:31,349
The two-year fell in tandem.

8
00:00:31,349 --> 00:00:37,280
The entire move was powered by a repricing of the Fed path, not by fresh economic data.

9
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,902
Let me unpack the Fed decision.

10
00:00:39,902 --> 00:00:43,824
The FOMC hiked twenty-five basis points.

11
00:00:43,824 --> 00:00:46,422
The dot plot came in hawkish.

12
00:00:46,422 --> 00:00:48,873
No terminal rate was given.

13
00:00:48,873 --> 00:00:51,263
No promise of a pause.

14
00:00:51,263 --> 00:00:53,947
The presser lasted thirty minutes.

15
00:00:53,947 --> 00:00:56,594
One of the shortest in Fed history.

16
00:00:56,594 --> 00:01:00,000
Goldman expects another twenty-five in October.

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,856
Bank of America is more aggressive.

18
00:01:02,856 --> 00:01:06,091
They see hikes in both October and December.

19
00:01:06,091 --> 00:01:09,020
The tightening cycle is far from over.

20
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,753
Now here is the key divergence.

21
00:01:11,753 --> 00:01:14,228
The market did not sell off.

22
00:01:14,228 --> 00:01:16,594
Instead, it rallied.

23
00:01:16,594 --> 00:01:19,927
Three forces converged simultaneously.

24
00:01:19,927 --> 00:01:23,027
First, the hike was fully priced.

25
00:01:23,027 --> 00:01:25,834
The bad news became good news.

26
00:01:25,834 --> 00:01:30,013
Traders shifted from a tightening narrative to a resilience trade.

27
00:01:30,013 --> 00:01:33,616
Second, Middle East de-escalation is real.

28
00:01:33,616 --> 00:01:37,500
Saudi Arabia asked Oman to broker a ceasefire.

29
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:42,488
Trump plans to convene foreign leaders next week on post-conflict arrangements.

30
00:01:42,488 --> 00:01:46,679
Iran's foreign minister is in Beijing discussing the aftermath.

31
00:01:46,679 --> 00:01:49,277
Oil price upside is fading.

32
00:01:49,277 --> 00:01:52,206
Import inflation pressure is easing.

33
00:01:52,206 --> 00:01:56,300
That directly reduces the need for further aggressive tightening.

34
00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:01,226
Third, U.S. jobless claims fell to one hundred ninety-six thousand.

35
00:02:01,226 --> 00:02:03,150
A multi-year low.

36
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:07,010
The labor market shows low layoffs, low hiring.

37
00:02:07,010 --> 00:02:11,030
Companies are not cutting heads after AI cost savings.

38
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:16,741
They are reinvesting into new projects, raising wages, and expanding capex.

39
00:02:16,741 --> 00:02:19,535
That is uniquely American right now.

40
00:02:19,535 --> 00:02:22,929
Strong employment means no imminent recession.

41
00:02:22,929 --> 00:02:26,569
But it also means inflation stickiness persists.

42
00:02:26,569 --> 00:02:29,425
Higher for longer is the base case.

43
00:02:29,425 --> 00:02:31,471
One political note.

44
00:02:31,471 --> 00:02:34,106
Trump publicly supported the hike.

45
00:02:34,106 --> 00:02:37,292
He said he spoke with Powell before the decision.

46
00:02:37,292 --> 00:02:41,103
This is a sharp reversal from his usual rate-cut pressure.

47
00:02:41,103 --> 00:02:47,697
The reality is that with inflation well above two percent, forcing a cut would blow out expectations.

48
00:02:47,697 --> 00:02:50,773
The Fed is not bending to political pressure.

49
00:02:50,773 --> 00:02:55,895
Now let me connect this macro liquidity picture to where capital is actually flowing.

50
00:02:55,895 --> 00:03:00,466
The AI capex cycle is accelerating, not decelerating.

51
00:03:00,466 --> 00:03:05,172
OpenAI expects next year's product sales to be double this year's.

52
00:03:05,172 --> 00:03:08,616
That is a direct tailwind for the chip complex.

53
00:03:08,616 --> 00:03:12,243
Bank of America frames this as a prisoner's dilemma.

54
00:03:12,243 --> 00:03:19,951
No hyperscaler can hit the brakes without falling behind in model capability, compute reserves, and ecosystem lock-in.

55
00:03:19,951 --> 00:03:26,201
They project global AI capital expenditure could exceed three trillion dollars by 2027.

56
00:03:26,201 --> 00:03:29,143
UBS makes a critical distinction.

57
00:03:29,143 --> 00:03:33,469
Slower model iteration does not mean slower AI demand.

58
00:03:33,469 --> 00:03:37,770
Two-thirds of current compute demand comes from inference workloads.

59
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:40,540
Token usage is still compounding.

60
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:44,486
The bottleneck is shifting from chips to power infrastructure.

61
00:03:44,486 --> 00:03:53,322
Goldman now forecasts that by 2030, new U.S. data center electricity demand will equal the entire electricity consumption of a new Japan.

62
00:03:53,322 --> 00:04:00,135
The constraints are gas turbines, transformers, transmission lines, skilled labor, and permitting.

63
00:04:00,135 --> 00:04:05,233
South Korea's leadership publicly stated they will not slow the AI pace.

64
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:07,966
Barclays' core thesis is simple.

65
00:04:07,966 --> 00:04:14,425
As long as corporate earnings keep expanding, equities can absorb the valuation drag from higher rates.

66
00:04:14,425 --> 00:04:17,206
The financing structure is changing.

67
00:04:17,206 --> 00:04:22,819
AI companies are increasingly tapping five-year medium-term notes to fund capex.

68
00:04:22,819 --> 00:04:25,197
That is a structural shift.

69
00:04:25,197 --> 00:04:30,736
It adds selling pressure to the intermediate Treasury market and amplifies rate volatility.

70
00:04:30,736 --> 00:04:36,116
Meanwhile, AI safety advocates are pushing for independent third-party audits.

71
00:04:36,116 --> 00:04:38,162
The tension is clear.

72
00:04:38,162 --> 00:04:42,072
Geopolitical competition demands full-speed AI.

73
00:04:42,072 --> 00:04:45,050
Safety regulation demands friction.

74
00:04:45,050 --> 00:04:48,101
Both cannot be true simultaneously.

75
00:04:48,101 --> 00:04:51,594
Now to the individual names driving today's tape.

76
00:04:51,704 --> 00:04:53,455
SpaceX.

77
00:04:53,405 --> 00:04:55,831
This is the story of the quarter.

78
00:04:55,831 --> 00:04:59,961
The stock is up nearly fifty percent from its late-August low.

79
00:04:59,961 --> 00:05:03,736
Morgan Stanley raised its target to three hundred dollars.

80
00:05:03,736 --> 00:05:09,054
Their split valuation shows the market is severely underwriting the AI business.

81
00:05:09,054 --> 00:05:12,952
The implied valuation on that segment is extremely low.

82
00:05:12,952 --> 00:05:15,488
There is massive re-rating room.

83
00:05:15,488 --> 00:05:19,765
Musk is pouring resources into AI compute infrastructure.

84
00:05:19,765 --> 00:05:26,567
The goal is a massive GPU cluster operational within 2026 to support Grok training at scale.

85
00:05:26,567 --> 00:05:31,101
That is a direct play on the inference demand thesis we just discussed.

86
00:05:31,101 --> 00:05:33,528
The merger narrative is real.

87
00:05:33,528 --> 00:05:40,856
Options data shows the probability of a Tesla-SpaceX combination by 2028 exceeds sixty-five percent.

88
00:05:40,856 --> 00:05:43,626
The logic is vertical integration.

89
00:05:43,626 --> 00:05:48,417
Chips, compute, energy, and space on one balance sheet.

90
00:05:48,417 --> 00:05:50,979
The obstacles are significant.

91
00:05:50,979 --> 00:05:58,123
Antitrust review, valuation disputes, Musk's governance structure, and defense-contractor regulations.

92
00:05:58,123 --> 00:06:00,905
But the optionality is pricing in.

93
00:06:00,905 --> 00:06:07,400
Additionally, SpaceX's inclusion in the Nasdaq index is pulling in billions in passive flows.

94
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:11,028
That is mechanical buying that compounds the momentum.

95
00:06:11,028 --> 00:06:12,461
Tesla.

96
00:06:12,461 --> 00:06:16,542
The stock is being re-rated through the SpaceX merger lens.

97
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:25,194
If the combination materializes, Tesla gains access to SpaceX's energy storage, satellite compute, and launch infrastructure.

98
00:06:25,194 --> 00:06:29,827
The standalone auto business is no longer the sole valuation driver.

99
00:06:29,827 --> 00:06:32,118
Watch the options market.

100
00:06:32,118 --> 00:06:36,113
The 2028 merger probability is the key metric.

101
00:06:36,113 --> 00:06:41,775
If that number creeps above seventy percent, expect a step-change in Tesla's multiple.

102
00:06:41,775 --> 00:06:45,452
Below sixty percent, the premium deflates.

103
00:06:45,452 --> 00:06:50,133
On the standalone front, the AI cost-savings narrative is holding.

104
00:06:50,133 --> 00:06:52,804
Tesla is not cutting headcount.

105
00:06:52,804 --> 00:06:57,155
It is redirecting savings into new product lines and capex.

106
00:06:57,155 --> 00:07:01,518
That aligns with the broader U.S. labor market pattern we discussed.

107
00:07:01,518 --> 00:07:06,297
The risk is that higher-for-longer rates compress auto financing demand.

108
00:07:06,297 --> 00:07:08,577
Watch the ten-year yield.

109
00:07:08,577 --> 00:07:15,623
If it reclaims five percent, consumer credit costs spike and that hits Tesla's delivery economics directly.

110
00:07:15,623 --> 00:07:19,214
For risk management, here are the levels to track.

111
00:07:19,214 --> 00:07:24,116
On the macro side, the ten-year at four point nine seven is the pivot.

112
00:07:24,116 --> 00:07:28,417
A break above five percent invalidates the short-squeeze rally.

113
00:07:28,417 --> 00:07:32,988
A hold below four point nine supports the risk-on continuation.

114
00:07:32,988 --> 00:07:38,417
On SpaceX, the three-hundred-dollar Morgan Stanley target is the near-term magnet.

115
00:07:38,417 --> 00:07:42,143
Support sits at the late-August consolidation zone.

116
00:07:42,143 --> 00:07:46,150
A close below that level signals the rally is exhausted.

117
00:07:46,150 --> 00:07:50,942
On Tesla, the merger probability in options is your leading indicator.

118
00:07:50,942 --> 00:07:53,809
Pair it with the Nasdaq index level.

119
00:07:53,809 --> 00:07:58,932
If the Nasdaq loses its recent breakout, the merger premium unwinds.

120
00:07:58,932 --> 00:08:00,721
The bottom line.

121
00:08:00,721 --> 00:08:03,589
This rally is a triple convergence.

122
00:08:03,589 --> 00:08:08,711
Hike landing, geopolitical easing, and AI earnings resilience.

123
00:08:08,711 --> 00:08:12,559
It is an expectation repair, not a trend reversal.

124
00:08:12,559 --> 00:08:15,525
The structural risks remain intact.

125
00:08:15,525 --> 00:08:18,123
Forty trillion in U.S. debt.

126
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:20,672
Persistent fiscal deficits.

127
00:08:20,672 --> 00:08:24,042
Oil above one hundred dollars in the base case.

128
00:08:24,042 --> 00:08:27,952
AI financing stress in the intermediate bond market.

129
00:08:27,952 --> 00:08:32,253
Crypto regulation stalled in the Senate at fifty to forty-nine.

130
00:08:32,253 --> 00:08:34,569
None of that has resolved.

131
00:08:34,569 --> 00:08:38,773
The Fed is in a 1997 Greenspan-style bind.

132
00:08:38,773 --> 00:08:40,562
No recession.

133
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:42,633
Sticky inflation.

134
00:08:42,633 --> 00:08:45,574
AI pushing the neutral rate higher.

135
00:08:45,574 --> 00:08:49,300
The tightening must continue without crushing the economy.

136
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:52,143
This is a long, grinding fight.

137
00:08:52,143 --> 00:08:57,130
The rally can persist, but it will be punctuated by violent mean-reversions.

138
00:08:57,130 --> 00:09:01,138
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

139
00:09:01,138 --> 00:09:05,304
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
